  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151148/assets/7f2467ce2b4c3e1a446b3fb50b88c77ad70db02293f7f8a8f76ba4bd718bebdb.png)\n\nFor the diagram shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The segments $\\overset{―}{DB}$ and $\\overset{―}{BE}$ are not congruent\n\nII. $\\overset{―}{AD}≅\\overset{―}{BE}$\n\nIII. $CE\\ne 5\\,\\text{cm}$",
  "worked_solution": "- Statement I is false. According to the picture, we have that both $\\overset{―}{DB}$ and $\\overset{―}{BE}$ have the same hash marks, so\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{DB}≅\\overset{―}{BE}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the picture, we have that $\\overset{―}{AD}$ and $\\overset{―}{BE}$ have different hash marks, so\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AD}≇\\overset{―}{BE}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. According to the picture, we have that $\\overset{―}{BE}$ and $\\overset{―}{CE}$ have different hash marks, so\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{BE}≇\\overset{―}{CE}.\n$$\n\nHence, $BE\\ne CE,$ and since $BE=5\\,\\text{cm}$, we have $CE\\ne 5\\,\\text{cm}.$,\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true.",
